    (8, None, '\'A real chef does not trust strangers.\' "Doveryat", to trust, has "vera", faith, inside it. "Chuzhoy" means \'someone else\'s\', so "chuzhie lyudi" are strangers, and after "doveryat" they become "chuzhim lyudyam", \'to strangers\'.'),
    (9, None, '\'May I go with you?\' "Mozhno mne", literally \'possible to me\', is the standard way to ask permission. "Poekhat" means going by car, not on foot.'),
